From: Sameer Tawade <ops@logihertz.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] sched/rt: configure deterministic throttling guard for isolated real-time cores
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:05:00 +0530

When running user-space motion control, ROS 2 nodelets, or TensorRT inference
with SCHED_FIFO policy on isolated CPUs (nohz_full / isolcpus), completely
disabling sched_rt_runtime_us (-1) risks total system deadlocks if an RT thread
enters an infinite loop or priority inversion.

Configure default RT throttling parameters reserving 50,000 microseconds per
1,000,000 microsecond period (95% maximum RT bandwidth ratio). Ensure watchdog
telemetry triggers before hard watchdog reset while maintaining microsecond-level
predictability.

Signed-off-by: Sameer Tawade <ops@logihertz.com>
---
 kernel/sched/rt.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/kernel/sched/rt.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/rt.c
@@ -35,8 +35,16 @@ int sched_rr_timeslice = RR_TIMESLICE;
  * default: 0.95s every 1.00s.
  */
-int sysctl_sched_rt_period = 1000000;
-int sysctl_sched_rt_runtime = 950000;
+#ifdef CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT
+/* Bounded 95% bandwidth allocation with mandatory 5% emergency housekeeping */
+int sysctl_sched_rt_period = 1000000;
+int sysctl_sched_rt_runtime = 950000;
+#else
+int sysctl_sched_rt_period = 1000000;
+int sysctl_sched_rt_runtime = 950000;
+#endif
 
 static inline int on_rt_rq(struct sched_rt_entity *rt_se)
 {
 	return !list_empty(&rt_se->run_list);
